WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.150
One ocean covers 71 per
cent of Earth's surface.

2
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.570
It holds about 97 per
cent of Earth's water:

3
00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:11.830
about 1.33 billion cubic kilometres of it.

4
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.270
And it is not spread evenly.

5
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:19.150
The Southern Hemisphere is so watery
it may be called the water hemisphere.

6
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.750
Now pull the plug.

7
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:25.290
Let the water drain away, until
the bare sea floor lies open.

8
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.530
What landscape would you see down there?

9
00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:29.750
Just a flat, muddy plain?

10
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.870
In this mission, you'll measure the ocean,

11
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.350
and map where it is deep
and where it is shallow.

12
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:40.550
Then you'll find out how moving plates
and slow sinking build the hidden relief.

13
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:44.750
Your mission: find out what landscape
lies hidden on the sea floor.
